## Configuration

Settings come from environment variables only. See [docs/configuration.md](docs/configuration.md).

| Variable | Default | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `HOST` | `127.0.0.1` | Address to listen on (`0.0.0.0` in a container) |
| `PORT` | `8080` | Port to listen on (`0` picks a free one) |
| `LOG_LEVEL` | `info` | `debug`, `info`, `warn` or `error` |
| `SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT` | `10s` | How long in-flight requests get after a stop signal |

## Development

Requires Go, make, curl, a C compiler (for the race detector) and [golangci-lint](https://golangci-lint.run/). templ runs through `go tool`, so it needs no separate install.

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `make generate` | Regenerate `*_templ.go` from the `.templ` components |
| `make serve` | Build and run the server in the foreground |
| `make test` | Unit, component and handler tests with the race detector |
| `make test-integration` | Run the built binary, load pages and post forms, including signal shutdown |
| `make lint` | golangci-lint |
| `make htmx` | Download the latest htmx release into `static/vendor/` |
| `make ci` | Everything CI runs |

See [docs/DEVELOPMENT.md](docs/DEVELOPMENT.md) for setup and scoped tests, [docs/ARCHITECTURE.md](docs/ARCHITECTURE.md) for where code goes, and [docs/pages.md](docs/pages.md) for how pages, forms and htmx responses behave.

